    3. For each marker color, pick an anchor row such that its glyph fits in rows 0-19 (anchor >= |min_dr|, anchor + max_dr <= 19) and no two expanded glyphs share any cell
    4. Render expanded glyphs onto a 20x20 bg grid with frame bars — this is the OUTPUT
    5. Choose 1 additional glyph color (from {1,2,3,6,7}, distinct from markers and frame) as the "example glyph" to show in the INPUT
    6. Pick an anchor row for the example glyph that fits in grid and doesn't collide with marker anchor pixels (the 2-pixel pairs that remain in input)
    7. Build INPUT = frame + example glyph rendered + marker pairs (erase the expanded marker content, keep only the 2 endpoint pixels per marker)
